            "is_free": false,
            "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to OFS.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are a freight operator in the busiest orbital depot in the galaxy. Your contract is simple: survive five one-minute shifts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three conveyor belts feed your cabin without stopping. Normal cargo passes through. Suspicious packages appear. Three little intruders try to reach you. Read the belts, manage your energy, and stay operational to the end of each shift.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A perfect run lasts only five minutes. Surviving one is another story.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Purge suspicious packages</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fire the EMP Purge to destroy suspicious packages before they reach your cabin. The more you purge at once, the more bounty you earn. One package is safe. Three is profitable. Five is probably a terrible idea — and a very good payout.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage your energy</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The EMP Purge, the Brake, and the Security Shutter all drain energy, and it never regenerates on its own. Request batteries at the right moment, or end your shift with a dead system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Block the intruders</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three little intruders claw at your cabin, each with its own path, timing, and warning signs. The Security Shutter stops them — but every second it stays down costs energy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stay medically covered</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An accident doesn't always end the run. OFS calls it a &quot;work incident.&quot; You have limited medical coverage; when it hits zero, you're done. Renew your insurance between shifts to stay in the contract.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hack the system</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After every shift, OFS rolls out a new corporate measure: weaker batteries, more suspicious cargo, disabled warnings, higher conveyor pressure. Between shifts, a black market terminal lets you fight back — cut your EMP cost, upgrade your batteries, ease the pressure, or gamble on bigger multi-clear payouts. Every upgrade can save your run. Every bad choice can ruin it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What to expect</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Five one-minute shifts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Short, hard, replayable runs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three conveyor belts to watch</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Suspicious packages to purge with precise timing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bounty rewards for multi-clears</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three cartoon intruders to block</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Limited energy, no passive regen</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Medical insurance to renew between shifts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A black market hacking terminal</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cold, absurd corporate satire</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >OFS does not need you to be a hero.<br>OFS needs you to be profitable.</p>",
            "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to OFS.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are a freight operator in the busiest orbital depot in the galaxy. Your contract is simple: survive five one-minute shifts.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three conveyor belts feed your cabin without stopping. Normal cargo passes through. Suspicious packages appear. Three little intruders try to reach you. Read the belts, manage your energy, and stay operational to the end of each shift.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A perfect run lasts only five minutes. Surviving one is another story.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Purge suspicious packages</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fire the EMP Purge to destroy suspicious packages before they reach your cabin. The more you purge at once, the more bounty you earn. One package is safe. Three is profitable. Five is probably a terrible idea — and a very good payout.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Manage your energy</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The EMP Purge, the Brake, and the Security Shutter all drain energy, and it never regenerates on its own. Request batteries at the right moment, or end your shift with a dead system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Block the intruders</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three little intruders claw at your cabin, each with its own path, timing, and warning signs. The Security Shutter stops them — but every second it stays down costs energy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Stay medically covered</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An accident doesn't always end the run. OFS calls it a &quot;work incident.&quot; You have limited medical coverage; when it hits zero, you're done. Renew your insurance between shifts to stay in the contract.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hack the system</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After every shift, OFS rolls out a new corporate measure: weaker batteries, more suspicious cargo, disabled warnings, higher conveyor pressure. Between shifts, a black market terminal lets you fight back — cut your EMP cost, upgrade your batteries, ease the pressure, or gamble on bigger multi-clear payouts. Every upgrade can save your run. Every bad choice can ruin it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What to expect</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Five one-minute shifts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Short, hard, replayable runs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three conveyor belts to watch</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Suspicious packages to purge with precise timing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bounty rewards for multi-clears</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three cartoon intruders to block</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Limited energy, no passive regen</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Medical insurance to renew between shifts</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A black market hacking terminal</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cold, absurd corporate satire</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >OFS does not need you to be a hero.<br>OFS needs you to be profitable.</p>",
